{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>They have provoked me.</b> The ayin is light to ease pronunciation." "<b>With a no-el.</b> The meaning: it has no power to save." "<b>With their vanities.</b> And not with a true thing." "<b>I will provoke them.</b> From the heavy additional binyan, and it yields two actions." "<b>A no-people.</b> For they are not my people. And behold, he explained how he will bring it about — that he will bring upon them alone extraordinary troubles, and more than everything." "<b>A vile nation.</b> For the fool and the vile one knows nothing, and therefore he kills and does not spare."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:02.108049935Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}